## Structure (layers)

Each module is self-contained and stacks three layers top to bottom:

```
src/modules/<module>/
├── <module>.controller.ts   ← HTTP layer: routing, request/response
├── <module>.service.ts      ← business logic
├── <module>.repository.ts   ← data access
├── dto/                     ← request shapes
├── entities/                ← the model
└── <module>.module.ts       ← NestJS wiring
```

Call direction: `controller` → `service` → `repository`. A layer only ever talks to the one directly below it.

The repository is currently in-memory. To move to a real database, change the repository implementation only — the service and controller stay untouched.

